<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>go-authn – Keys</title><link>https://go-authn.github.io/docs/0.11/tags/keys/</link><description>Recent content in Keys on go-authn</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://go-authn.github.io/docs/0.11/tags/keys/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>pkcs12 — the key and certificates inside a .p12 upload</title><link>https://go-authn.github.io/docs/0.11/libraries/pkcs12/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://go-authn.github.io/docs/0.11/libraries/pkcs12/</guid><description>
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What private key and certificates are inside this file somebody sent us?&lt;/strong&gt;
PKCS#12 (&lt;a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7292" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;RFC 7292&lt;/a&gt;) is the &lt;code&gt;.p12&lt;/code&gt; /&lt;code&gt;.pfx&lt;/code&gt; container an exporter writes a key, its certificate and the rest of the
chain into. &lt;code&gt;golang.org/x/crypto/pkcs12&lt;/code&gt; is deprecated and frozen on SHA-1 and
3DES/RC2, so it rejects what OpenSSL 3 and 4 and current Windows write by
default (PBES2, AES, SHA-2 MACs). This module reads those, with no dependency
beyond the standard library, and is built for &lt;strong&gt;untrusted uploads&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;go get github.com/go-authn/pkcs12@v0.1.1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
